  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 机\ntitle: desk; writing table\njlpt: 2\ntags: [jlpt-n2, grade-6, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 6\nradical: 木\nradicalNumber: 75\nonyomi: [キ]\nkunyomi: [つくえ]\ndistractors: [札, 九, 村]\n---\n\n# 机 — desk; writing table\n\n**Strokes:** 6 · **Key (radical):** 木 (no. 75) · **JLPT:** N2 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n机 concerns a desk or table used for activities such as writing or studying. The independent native noun is 机 つくえ. 机上 きじょう literally concerns being on a desk and also has theoretical or not-yet-implemented uses.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic, not etymology:** Notice 木 beside the 几-like right-hand shape and imagine a wooden writing desk. This is a modern-shape memory aid, not a verified origin.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| キ | on | 机上 きじょう - on the desk; theoretical |\n| つくえ | kun | [机](../words/机.md) つくえ - desk |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [机](../words/机.md) つくえ - desk\n- 机上 きじょう - on the desk; theoretical\n\n## Notes\n\n- The standalone noun 机 is read つくえ; キ is illustrated here by the compound 机上, not offered as a replacement for that noun's ordinary pronunciation.\n- The English word table is broader than a writing desk. Use the established Japanese name for a particular kind of furniture rather than translating every table as 机.\n- 机上の きじょうの can qualify something theoretical; an abstract proposal need not be physically sitting on a desk.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project), 2026-10-21 snapshot. Word pairs: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1220210, 1220220.\n",
